============================================================

Each Budget Plan must use exactly one Category Scope:

    ALL
    SELECTED

------------------------------------------------------------
ALL CATEGORIES MODE
------------------------------------------------------------

When Category Scope is:

    ALL

the Budget Plan includes every CURRENT valid broad Category available through
Category Manager.

Do NOT store a copied list of all Categories in the Budget Plan config.

Instead, store only that the plan uses:

    category_scope = "all"

When the Budget Plan is refreshed, re-read the CURRENT Category Manager and use
all valid broad Categories that exist at that time.

This behavior is intentionally dynamic.

Example:

At plan creation Category Manager contains:

    Food
    Household
    Automotive

The plan uses ALL.

Later the user adds:

    Home Improvement

to Category Manager.

On the next Budget Plan refresh, Home Improvement must automatically be included
without editing the Budget Plan config.

This is required behavior.

------------------------------------------------------------
SELECTED CATEGORIES MODE
------------------------------------------------------------

When Category Scope is:

    SELECTED

the Budget Plan includes only the specific broad Categories saved in that plan.

N means any positive number of currently valid broad Categories.

Example:

    Categories:
        Food
        Household
        Personal Care

Only purchases belonging to one of those saved Categories count toward the
Budget Plan.

The user must select Categories from the CURRENT validated broad Category list
derived from Category Manager.

Do not ask the user to type Category names manually.

Display the current Categories as a numbered selection list.

